{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1409","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Decrease the Sum of Digits"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a positive integer $$$n$$$. In one move, you can increase $$$n$$$ by one (i.e. make $$$n := n + 1$$$). Your task is to find the minimum number of moves you need to perform in order to make the sum of digits of $$$n$$$ be less than or equal to $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to answer $$$t$$$ independent test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains one integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2 \\cdot 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. Then $$$t$$$ test cases follow."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of the test case contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$s$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^{18}$$$; $$$1 \\le s \\le 162$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print the answer: the minimum number of moves you need to perform in order to make the sum of digits of $$$n$$$ be less than or equal to $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":